Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:04.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Imagine… you get struck by lightning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.40,0:00:06.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What would happen to your body?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.60,0:00:10.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You are standing in an open field.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.50,0:00:12.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The air smells like metal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.50,0:00:15.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Your hair… starts to rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.60,0:00:18.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.80,0:00:21.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Three hundred million volts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.40,0:00:27.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In a split second, the air around you heats to thirty thousand degrees.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.00,0:00:30.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Five times hotter than the surface of the Sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.10,0:00:33.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The rain on your skin turns to steam.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.90,0:00:36.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Your shoes can be blown right off.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.60,0:00:40.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}And your heart… stops.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.10,0:00:48.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But often, most of the current flashes over your skin, not through you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.10,0:00:50.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It leaves a strange mark.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.20,0:00:57.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}A red, fern-like pattern, called a Lichtenberg figure.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.80,0:01:02.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}With fast help, nine out of ten people survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.80,0:01:07.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}One park ranger was struck seven times… and lived.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.00,0:01:09.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}So remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.40,0:01:13.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}If you can hear thunder… you are close enough to be struck.
